 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? Gosh is short for something big, generous with an emotional impact. It describes how someone feels about something. Kind of. Watercolour makes it wet and colour means the colours you use with paintbrushes or pens. Acrylic dries fast and is good for details and lines. It is, though it can be quite forgiving too. A simple layer of white at the start gives you lots of space if that's what you need. Honestly, the sky first. It gives you something lovely to work on and helps with your mood. Try to make it look like that, yes. Big bold lines and bright colours.",
